Ok, you are plain right; there's a WLAN/BT combo.

Here goes the full lsusb -v output.

In my tests the only modules loaded are from the WLAN interface, that
is:

insmod ./compat/compat.ko
insmod ./compat/sch_codel.ko
insmod ./compat/sch_fq_codel.ko
modprobe rfkill
insmod ./net/wireless/cfg80211.ko
insmod ./net/mac80211/mac80211.ko
insmod ./drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath.ko
insmod ./drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath9k/ath9k_hw.ko
insmod ./drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath9k/ath9k_common.ko
insmod ./drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath9k/ath9k.ko debug=0xffffffff
nohwcrypt=1 blink=1 btcoex_enable=1

rfkill is taken from the stock kernel from Slackware 13.37, that is,
2.6.38-4-smp, 32-bit version.

Even being ath9k.ko loaded with debug=0xffffffff, this actually is not
effective as the original kernel isn't configured to allow debug. The
messages provided in an earlier post are from printk()'s included by
myself.

Thanks,

Luiz

